 be able to offer the first commercial  click to the ploy offering today if you  go to the Google cloud site you will  find that they're a bunch of click to  deploy offerings out there all open  source where you can go and very quickly  click on an offering and it'd take a  couple of make a couple of configuration  settings and then launch it and it just  saves a whole lot of steps in  configuration and we're going to be  offering that you'll also be able very  soon to start doing things where you  take a whole bunch of resources in a  similar way you can say I want to fire  up three instances I want to use this  storage I want to push it to fastly and  you can do it all through essentially  one configuration script you'll be able  to do that very soon too so that once  you have your settings the way you want  them you can just fire it off the same  way every time  speaking of fastly we're also going to  be offering fastly integration soon so  today you can do it there are a few  steps involved we're gonna make it a lot  easier the simple way is you there are  two ways you can do it really the first  way is if you have a live stream you can  push it to a storage bucket makes it  very easy and then fastly just picks it  up from there and distributes globally  we also have very low latency  connections because fastly is co-located  where or has the interconnects where  Google cloud platform is located so the  the connections there are really low  latency which is very good for us as far  as getting content to your users faster  so the TV they don't hear the cheer on  the TV you know several seconds before  they see it on their device and then the  last thing is if you're doing on-demand  streaming and you're pulling the content  off of a Google compute engine instance  using fastly as your distribution  mechanism as Simon mentioned earlier  they have the origin shield capability  which protects the origin from getting  too many requests at once from all those  edge nodes that vastly wrongs they just  have a single request come back all the  time and then feed all those nodes and  so that workflow that I showed you  earlier would look like this when you  put fastly in the middle so that's it if  you have questions we'll have Q&amp;A later  I'll be happy to answer them and first  I'll stick around also as well if you  have other questions or feel free to  email
 

